# What `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# Without this file gcloud infers the list from .gitignore, which is a different file written for a
# different purpose — it happens to cover .env today, and nothing keeps it doing so. The build
# context is the one place a local .env would leave this machine, so the exclusion is stated here
# rather than inherited.
#
# .dockerignore covers what lands in the IMAGE; this covers what leaves the machine at all. They
# overlap on purpose.

# --- credentials and local state: never upload -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
.dev.vars
google-client.json
ada-auth.db
.ada/
.cos0/

# --- not needed to build the server ------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
.git
.github
bench
docs
test
skills
scratchpad
out
out-*
runs/
.wrangler/
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
